  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Just Kissed My Baby -$** (1 other source): Robert Randolph plays pedal steel guitar on this song, alongside Ivan Neville on vocals [1]\n- **James Brown Medley: Lickin' Stick/There Was A Time/I Got You/Get Up Off Of That Thing/Get On The Good Foot/I Feel All Right *#@|** (1 other source): The medley features James Casey and Blake Hillard on horns, Nigel Hall on vocals and Ivan Neville on keys [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Alan Evans intro, talking about opening bands**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Nigel speaks**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Yesterday**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **I'll Never Know**: rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **A Song For You**: rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **I Love You More Than You'll Ever Know**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **banter - Alan speaks and invites out Shady Horns**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **banter - thanking Nigel, setbreak announce**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Everybody Wants To Rule The World [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2010-03-06** (recommended): audience recording; 32 songs; 183 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Most of the audience chatted constantly through Nigel Hall's set, and the recording picks up that crowd noise [1]\n- **soulive2010-03-06.tlm170.flac24**: audience recording; 32 songs; 183 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: crowd/Robert Randolph [1]\n- Ryan Zoidas and Sam Kininger add saxophones on several songs, and Ivan Neville sings with the band on others [1]\n- Danny Sadownick joins on percussion for Hatrick, Got Soul, Hercules, Jesus Children Of America and If You Want Me To Stay [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2010-03-06**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [1]\n- **soulive2010-03-06.tlm170.flac24**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [2]. Also: This is the 24-bit version of the recording, not meant for CD burning or MP3 streaming; a 16-bit copy exists [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by www.primevideo.com: [Prime Video: Bowlive: Live at the Brooklyn Bowl](https://www.primevideo.com/-/es/detail/0JRU3HG1LVE7ZHVZUBD69H63AS) [7]",
